Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["General expression", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.872757918910462*^9, 3.87275792337864*^9}, {
   3.872760381089493*^9, 3.872760381823805*^9}, {3.873629352662136*^9, 
   3.8736293554755774`*^9}, {3.893777961225232*^9, 3.893777964436627*^9}, 
   3.893778000959651*^9},ExpressionUUID->"b788c257-0d60-41f3-be67-\
128831c25efd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The below is taken from Andrew\[CloseCurlyQuote]s notebook. The spherical \
harmonics can be factored out. Expressed in Kinnersley tetrad, where blue \
indices are tetrad indices (1,2,3,4) = (l,n,m,mb). As it assumes mostly \
positive convention, need to add a minus sign. For this to make sense, also \
need the input to be in mostly negative convention!\nAssuming a Fourier \
series expansion in t.\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Mu]", "n", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2156ff9f-20f0-40a7-8b22-1d07467070b9"],
 " := ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"l", "+", "n"}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"l", "-", "n", "+", "1"}], ")"}]}]], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"2ae1049e-cd9c-49e1-bd8a-f54d46ec479c"],
 ". ,1 in green means derivative wrt to radius R (usual Schwarzschild \
coordinates).\nThe list of dG is  {ll,ln,lm,lmb,nn,nm,nmb,mm,mmb,mbmb}. \
\[Omega]1 = m \[CapitalOmega].\nThe metric has been expanded in frequency of \
exp(-i\[Omega]t). To use null tetrad representation, we want \
exp(-i\[Omega]u), where u=t-r*."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8736288666753693`*^9, 3.873628956575698*^9}, {
  3.873628988808755*^9, 3.8736291143472633`*^9}, {3.873643943616372*^9, 
  3.873643987685309*^9}, {3.87379059401873*^9, 3.873790597740472*^9}, {
  3.878535280790183*^9, 3.878535304612356*^9}, {3.883804653023693*^9, 
  3.883804725704637*^9}, {3.888392429279871*^9, 3.888392430254093*^9}, {
  3.898690383320201*^9, 
  3.898690459167596*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"359f231f-153f-438b-ac80-\
7d4aaec53cda"],

